Z||000014||BAM-BAM||01-26-2001||11:46 PM|||| Come on now folks! When this first started there were many people willing to help, now it's like everyone has amnesia. I did my part a couple times over and then a little. If every one was to donate only $10.00 it would be more than enough to help this family out. Put yourself in this guy's shoes, how much better would you feel if a group of complete strangers came to your aid in your time of need. Like has already been said, this little token won't break any of us but will make a world of difference to some one else. That's what we are and that's what we do. It's obvious that we aren't in the mainstream, we're a little different than most and I mean that in the most positive way. Look at how we share our experiences and knowledge so freely on this forum. There's not a trick or a secret that we wont share with another member; That's WHO WE ARE! When another member is in need of parts, there is a congragation of fellow members fighting over the right to be the one that helps; That's WHAT WE DO! WE are the crossection of the world that helps all others. Let's take this opportunity to both give and receive in one small guesture. It doesn't even amount to $.50 a day. $10.00, that's all. If you cant do that, then $5.00 or $2.00 anything will help. In the end it is this community that bennifits. We can rest comfortably knowing that we put out our collective hand and made a difference in someones life. That, in itself, could be the impetus to a quick recovery for Anthony. This is the best group of people in the world. Let's show what we can do to make a difference. Don't hesitate or say, "I'll do it tomorrow". Do it NOW! Write that cheque, have it ready for the USPS, or others, tomorrow. Let's show the Barber family what it means to have a since of community and pride of ownership as it relates to our Fiero's and anyone who has the good since to own one. Thanks for the space and GOD bless  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>  Peace, BAM-BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 01-26-2001).]||||reg||1
